{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths","id":1156813,"title":"Homebrew some Lower Depths!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-07T15:36:24-08:00","id":1156813,"title":"Homebrew some Lower Depths!","content":"So...each Lower Depth is as far away from the Supernal World as anything <i>can</i> be, and each such Lower Depth <i>lacks</i> a fundamental aspect of being. Duat lacks Sekhem and souls. The Inferno lacks Virtue. The nameless realm of the Strix lacks Vitae.<br /> <br /> So...why not make up a few of our own? Feel free to create a few Lower Depths and post them here, for all to see! (I, myself, will do so tomorrow, as an offline friend is coming over and I won\u2019t have the opportunity to do so today.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T16:02:52-08:00","id":1156823,"title":"","content":"I think this may have been done before? I'm pretty sure I posted a few concepts previously. I'll see if I can find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-07-2017, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T01:31:15-08:00","id":1156923,"title":"","content":"Not 100% homebrew because these are just non-canonical takes on canon places :<br /> <br /> The &quot;True Material World&quot; from Summoners could be seen as one lacking the Life Arcanum so everything is purely material here (this Lower Depth only feed on Life when living things go there and the planes kind of do that too if they are malevolent)<br /> <br /> The world of the Men in Black from the same book could also be a Lower Depth, this time lacking at least the magical part of Prime, maybe the MIB are so alien and obviously fake because they are are not humans or lacking wider aspects of the Arcanum of Truth. (Obviously they destroy magic when they are in the Fallen World by lobomotizing mages until they can't use magic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:00:33-08:00","id":1156974,"title":"","content":"I personally always found the Inferno as a really lame Lower Depths. The things that were shown in the Summoners book seemed far more inhuman/alien then the sort of thing that the Inferno usually held. Demons are just too... human? Eh. I mean, an evil spirit is also known as... you know? Any regular spirit of a vice? No need to make a special brand of it. But that's just my opinion, and I'd like to contribute positively, as well as negatively. So:<br /> <br /> I did have some random ideas, though. For instance, one of the silly, not going to do it but it interests me, Mage-Origin-of-Supernatural-Creature things I did once was that Vampires were first created (or each time each Clan was created) by a Lower Depths creature from a realm where dead flesh was all that existed. It took life and replaced it with a hunger for life, and an ability to spread like an infection, a parasite. As a being it was a nullity, pale and grey and sickly and bloated, not even shaped like a person. Just a fat, bloated tick of an impossible monster in a place without Life, but also without Matter. Everything was dead flesh that had never lived and never would live. <br /> <br /> Another idea for a creature I had was a being from a realm without Fate, in which all things worked according to schema, according to inexorable laws for which there was no room for minds either, honestly. The Seers used it to rip away the Fate from people. Both enemies to get rid of dangerous Destinies... but also their own agents. An agent without fate lacks this vital spark. They cannot imagine another world, they have trouble regaining willpower and making motivations, etc, etc. But they cannot be seen using the Fate Arcana. They are a nullity in the tapestry of Fate, though not in Mind/other Arcana. So such Seer Agents are often Sleepwalkers, given tools and loaded down with magic and then sent as assassins that can ambush and surprise enemy Acanthus, or more than them if you have the right defensive magic shoved into them. <br /> <br /> It also inspired a Seer Legacy that involved stealing the Fates from people (both Destiny Merits, and that special fatedness that courses through all lives in the CoD) and then burning it up as fuel for spells/Destiny merits for yourself, etc, etc. So a sort of Reaper of Fate kinda thing, all inspired by study of this horrific, Fate-Devouring being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:09:10-08:00","id":1156977,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Chthonic beings of the Underworld. Typically, it seems like Lower Depths only lack a certain part of an arcana\u2019s purview rather than the whole thing.<br /> <br /> For instance rather than missing Life, a Lower Depth might be missing healing. Existence is a horrible cannibalization of patchwork parts just to stay alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:16:17-08:00","id":1156979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1156977#post1156977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the Chthonic beings of the Underworld. Typically, it seems like Lower Depths only lack a certain part of an arcana\u2019s purview rather than the whole thing.<br /> <br /> For instance rather than missing Life, a Lower Depth might be missing healing. Existence is a horrible cannibalization of patchwork parts just to stay alive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe so, and that could be an interesting take on things, but I do think that there's benefit in the Fate-lacking idea. For one, in making it it helped me consider things from a different perspective. I don't believe in Fate, IRL. I don't think there are destinies/etc, etc. But in imagining a world where people have Fates, and that's a fundamental part of existence, it more clearly allowed me to imagine a human without fate in such a system (without going, 'Oh, you mean like RL humans?' or whatnot). <br /> <br /> Which led me to the conclusion/headcanon that just like having a life (Life), having a mind (Mind), and having a soul (Death), having a place in the tapestry of fate (Fate) was a necessary part of being human (and thus worthy of Imperium, etc, etc, Silver Ladder 4 Lyfe!). Thus having it taken away would have similar effects as being killed, having your mind destroyed, or losing your soul. <br /> <br /> All that said, a Lower Depth without Healing does sound appropriately grotesque and cool. So go for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:52:50-08:00","id":1157007,"title":"","content":"It appears you\u2019ve failed to grasp my meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:13:57-08:00","id":1157014,"title":"","content":"I took inspiration from Magic The Gathering for this idea. Specifically, the Shards of Alara, a world that was split into five pieces, each one missing two types of magic that are otherwise omnipresent in the multiverse. <br /> For the Fate-less place, I took my favorite plane, Esper. It's a realm where nothing is mutable, and order rules. Life is sickly here, so they infuse their bodies with a magical metal to enhance their frail forms in a world without true vitality. The big catch for my interpretation, is that it's a Lower Depth with 2 things missing. The first is naturally an aspect of Life, which is biodiversity and organic evolution. The 2nd, is artificially induced by its ruler, an immortal Sphinx named Sharuum; she steals the Fate from souls in order to give her ultimate free will, and all others are subjugated to her to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:44:54-08:00","id":1157077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157007#post1157007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears you\u2019ve failed to grasp my meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is? I mean, I personally didn't really notice a 'typical' when it came to Lower Depths beings. The lacking something, yes? But the idea that it should 'typically' only be one part of an Arcana isn't something I've actually noticed in anything I've read about Lower Depths beings?<br /> <br /> So no, I didn't fail to grasp your meaning. I just, you know, didn't agree with you? Basically, I haven't noticed the pattern you seem to have noticed, and won't be restricting myself to it, while at the same time the idea you had wasn't bad and it's fine if your headcanon is that it <b>has</b> to be one aspect of one arcana missing.Just don't expect everyone to agree. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","user":"The_Laurent","date":". 11-08-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T12:13:09-08:00","id":1157086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157077#post1157077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is? I mean, I personally didn't really notice a 'typical' when it came to Lower Depths beings. The lacking something, yes? But the idea that it should 'typically' only be one part of an Arcana isn't something I've actually noticed in anything I've read about Lower Depths beings?<br /> <br /> So no, I didn't fail to grasp your meaning. I just, you know, didn't agree with you? Basically, I haven't noticed the pattern you seem to have noticed, and won't be restricting myself to it, while at the same time the idea you had wasn't bad and it's fine if your headcanon is that it <b>has</b> to be one aspect of one arcana missing.Just don't expect everyone to agree. </div> </div> </div> </div>This is a better response to what I was saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T12:52:03-08:00","id":1157101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1156974#post1156974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally always found the Inferno as a really lame Lower Depths. The things that were shown in the Summoners book seemed far more inhuman/alien then the sort of thing that the Inferno usually held. Demons are just too... human? Eh. I mean, an evil spirit is also known as... you know? Any regular spirit of a vice? No need to make a special brand of it. But that's just my opinion, and I'd like to contribute positively, as well as negatively. So:</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Yeah. This is the result of Mage not having a line Developer at the time, and so two different versions of the Lower Depths both being mentioned in multiple books. There's the Inferno/Imperial Mysteries version, where it's pretty much just the Inferno, and there's the Summoners/Left Hand Path version, where it's strange alien worlds so far off comprehension and surviveability you can't go there.<br /> <br /> Along with &quot;The Supernal World is what you see in Mage Sight&quot;, fixing that by declaring one a subset of the other was my first day's work as Developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:30:36-08:00","id":1157110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1156974#post1156974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally always found the Inferno as a really lame Lower Depths. The things that were shown in the Summoners book seemed far more inhuman/alien then the sort of thing that the Inferno usually held. Demons are just too... human? Eh. I mean, an evil spirit is also known as... you know? Any regular spirit of a vice? No need to make a special brand of it. But that's just my opinion, and I'd like to contribute positively, as well as negatively.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow and spirits in general seem to have lessened in importance over time. Originally a place of gods and demons those have been corralled to other areas. It hasn't helped that there's incredibly few examples of high ranked spirits and how or what they do.<br /> <br /> But yes. There are evil spirits, and spirits of sin and vice. Currently, these and other spirits can become corrupted by the Inferno (they might be called Wounded, depending on what second edition does with Wounds and Inferno). At a glance, they're the same as spirits, but instead of just eating Resonant Essence, they work to corrupt things (mostly people) towards their Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T23:11:30-08:00","id":1157469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157110#post1157110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but instead of just eating Resonant Essence, they work to corrupt things (mostly people) towards their Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... most spirits do that too in order to create more resonant essence to feed from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T23:29:54-08:00","id":1157472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157469#post1157469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... most spirits do that too in order to create more resonant essence to feed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't really have a way to. Urging is one thing, but at that point you're just making it yourself. It's sort of like a contaminating feedback effect that supernaturally poisons the area or person or act. It was also, I guess the term would be, more efficient. It seemed to go directly to advancing their Rank more than feeding their Essence.<br /> <br /> But like you noted there's not much of a difference and (I imagine) the entire reasoning behind it seems to be just so you can have 'evil spirits from Hell,' and not 'what do you mean they're just spirits?' which I recall was a complaint about what the Crone might have been in Vampire the Requiem. Originally first edition seemed to have the Maeljin and their Maeltinet as straight up demons, judging by things like Lore of the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2017, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T06:49:05-08:00","id":1157517,"title":"","content":"To expand on what Flinty said, one of the classic examples of spirit ecology (written as an example) is of One Girl's Happiness. To make a long story short, it was formed as a mote when a girl was accepted into college. It used its powers to encourage her to take actions that made her happy, which led to it eventually being a spirit of the happiness that drugs and partying can bring, as the girl got into drinking to get that 'high' of happiness that the Spirit fed on, leading her entire life to be destroyed, until it reached the part where it possessed and took control of her. <br /> <br /> It was just a spirit doing what spirits do, acting in a manner alien to human interests and desires, one that sometimes can be 'benevolent' but is never inherently so in a human way, and I find that far more compelling than if you had an &quot;Evil Demon-Spirit of Addiction/Gluttony/etc&quot; that ruined her life because Teh Evulz. <br /> <br /> I mean, it would be interesting from a Hunter-level perspective if you had someone in the wrong. Like, they see this girl's life ruined by a spirit and they're religious and don't really know what spirits really are, so they make up this elaborate, &quot;Demon from hell, corrupting the innocent&quot; narrative, only to find that, no, that's not it at all. Etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:19:41-08:00","id":1157565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157469#post1157469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... most spirits do that too in order to create more resonant essence to feed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most spirits take an additive or consumptive approach to dealing with their competition \u2014 if they engage with other spirits, it's under the auspices of a derived relationship. (It's why magath are so messed up.)<br /> <br /> Wounded spirits don't incorporate their kills. The losing Resonance just goes nowhere because the spirit has become host to a hole in the fabric of the world's symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:16:42-08:00","id":1157607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157565#post1157565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most spirits take an additive or consumptive approach to dealing with their competition \u2014 if they engage with other spirits, it's under the auspices of a derived relationship. (It's why magath are so messed up.)<br /> <br /> Wounded spirits don't incorporate their kills. The losing Resonance just goes nowhere because the spirit has become host to a hole in the fabric of the world's symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that made it click.<br /> <br /> Immundi are ultimately creatures that embody disharmony and imbalance. They do not care, they only consume: natural Gluttony is all about getting enough resources to survive another winter, have some young, but Infernal Gluttony is about eating to deny others resources or because it is pleasurable. Normal Death recycles minerals, Infernal Death sterilizes the land. They kill for pleasure, not for food.<br /> <br /> But, to get on topic:<br /> <br /> The Numb: A realm that lacks pain completely, and with it, empathy or caution. It invades the world to hurt itself, and so actually get a good sense of what it is and capable of.<br /> <br /> The Bleak: A Depth that lacks Hope. Imagine a constant Lovecraftian story, this is that Earth-looking world. Depending on the inhabitant, it might invade to steal some actual quality of improvement to maintain stasis, or out of spite that even the Fallen World has more positive change than they do.<br /> <br /> The Searing: A realm that is missing darkness, physical or moral. Which sounds nice, except everything from there is blind due to light not impacting anything, and is at the complete mercy of the frequent natural disasters born from interaction with other depths, as it cannot comprehend the self enough for free will or survival instincts. Invaders tend to desire complete purification of the Fallen World, are corrupted by the allure of Vice, or worse, both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-10-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:47:41-08:00","id":1157627,"title":"","content":"So while the Lower Depths as whole are not specified around missing an Arcanum, but only certain aspects of reality, here are 11 realms with each being connected to one of the Arcana (and the Abyss) by being defined as lacking one of their aspects (including very rough names and description)-<br /> <br /> The Unwritten- lacks the concept of language and communication. Its denizens are all locked inside their minds, unable to interact with the outside world or each other in any meaningful way. When finding their way to the mortal world, they devour words, speech and communications in order to gain the pleasure of expressing themselves beyond their limited brains, dooming their victims to a hell made out of their own thoughts.<br /> <br /> The Crossroad- lacks the concept of direction. No matter where you go, you get to the same place. No matter which choice you make, you can move on. The demons who lurk in that dread realm are forever lost, unable to make any progress to achieve any goal they had in mind. Those shadow people and black dogs sometimes lost their way into the Fallen, where they consume directions and trap people in labyrinths from which there is no way out.<br /> <br /> The Winter- lacks the concept of warmth. Fire burns in that realm, but it freeze those which touch it. The sun shines, but its light is nothing more than the radiance of snow. In there, frost giants and snow ghosts roam to absorb every bit of heat which somehow fell to that icy realm. When they enter the physical world, the temperature immediately drops. Clouds cover the sun, and frost rise from the ground. Life is devoured by that cold, leaving nothing but frozen corpses.<br /> <br /> The Heresy- lacks the concept of worship. Nothing is holy in that realm, no ruler can tame its eternal chaos and only brute, physical strength is to be respected. Its demonic inhabitants are forever locked in blood struggles, betrayals and murders. When leaving their own private hell, they cause the system of faith to collapse upon themselves. Things which were once sacred lose their meaning, and nihilism celebrates its way to the world.<br /> <br /> The Rot- lacks the concept of healing. Everything in this realm is found in a constant state of decay. Every wound is deadly, every sickness means death. The whole world is a collection of rotten organisms, bound in constant pain as the very land screams in agony. When entering the Fallen, those spirits cause mass plagues and contaminated everything they touch. creating founds of fungi and faceless ooze.<br /> <br /> The Object- lacks the concept of metaphors and allegories. In that realm, what that is is what that is- items exist without any meaning, objects lacks any abstract principles to define them. Imagination is impossible to its denizens, seeing beyond their own world is impossible. That world, in fact, creates an almost identical image of the Fallen, only that nothing has a name, and nothing has a purpose. When entering the physical, those demons suffer from a trauma so great that they fall into a catatonic state. Around them, however, the world lose meaning- things no longer mean anything but their own physical form, and spiritual resonance fades and vanish without context.<br /> <br /> The Formless- lacks the concept of shape. It is an amorphous hell, where nothing has form and everything defies definition. Its natives are beings without form, ephemeral and hollow. No mortal mind can recognize them, for their appearance can not be defined through the sense. When entering the mortal world, everything lose its shape- the states of matter become unstable, the laws of physics shatter and entropy rise out of control while nothing can no longer be defined.<br /> <br /> The Eternal- lacks the concept of ending. Everything which ever started in this world lingers yet, degrading for all eternity without ever knowing rest. Those who inhabit that realm are ancient beings, birthed with the start of the universe, unable to die out, while their youngsters have turned the world to ever crowded. When they escape their damned world, they steal the ending of others, freezing life in the same moment and unable them to die out so they could bargain with that stolen death with others of their kind.<br /> <br /> The Chaos- lacks the concept of roles and purpose. There is no reason in that plane of existence- events happen without any correlation to each other, and there is no connection between cause and effect. The mad beings which lurk in that world exist only in the present, knowing that no matter the past, their future is forever undecided. When they manage to escape their prison, causality and probability go out of control. Grand wins and terrible loses await, the impossible becomes possible and the laws of newton turn null and void.<br /> <br /> The Sands- lacks the concept of memory. In that desert world, no one leaves any legacy behind- no shadows are cast under the sun, the steps are left in the sand, no tombstones are built in respect to the dead. No one remember anything which happened even a moment ago, and once death claims a victim they are being forgotten for all eternity. Those dust demons who roam that world have no history of their own, no stories to tell and no knowledge other than their instincts. Once they enter the Fallen, names degrade into nothing, memories vanish and lost items are never found again, as if they all were dust in the wind.<br /> <br /> The Ladder- lacks the concept of freedom. It is said that this realm was created from the ruins of the Celestial Ladder, as its foundations were cast to the depths of the world. In that realm, there is no such thing as free choice- everyone are born to a certain level of the ladder, and are forever bound to their place. The denizens of that realm are trapped in their position, and are unable to act outside of a very defined role and place in society. Those who are destined to leave their realm feed upon the freedom of others, turning them into nothing more than automata, and create a world where there is only one path open before any outcome, eliminating free will or alternative possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:19:30-08:00","id":1157637,"title":"","content":"I think there\u2019s actually a lore depth denizen that was in some book or other that would calm the Rot its home.<br /> <br /> The Eternal seems like a gone horribly right kind of way to achieve lichdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T13:55:50-08:00","id":1158268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157637#post1157637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Eternal seems like a gone horribly right kind of way to achieve lichdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That what you should think.<br /> <br /> When I made those sort writeups, I've wanted to emphasis the variance of the collection of worlds commonly known as the Depths. Some of the worlds were created to be directly aggressive toward life (like the Winter, the Rot and the Sand). Others were created to be horrifying, but as a consequence of them lacking a fundamental aspect of existence and not a malignant will (the Unwritten, the Crossroad and the Formless). One of them (the Object) was even made in a way which may generate sympathy toward its denizens (their presence in the Fallen is just as terrible for them as it is for those they feed upon, not to mention that they look perfectly human like- they just can't recognize that &quot;red&quot; means anything other than the color, or that if you call someone &quot;sweet&quot; it doesn't mean you should taste them). And some (the Heresy, the Chaos, the Ladder and the Eternal) were meant to be used- in case you are willing to suffer the consequences.<br /> <br /> Of those four, the Heresy is in fact the least dangerous one. If you summon one of those demons, the chances are that it would do exactly what you are asking for- destroying a certain system of faith. Sure, it may get out of control and ruin things you didn't want to ruin- but that's the risk at summoning any kind of spiritual being, be it from the Depths or not. The Heresy doesn't cheat or lies- it is brutally honest about what it wants, and if your interests align it would be your greatest ally. The Chaos is more dangerous, for it can only destroy probability- not direct it- making it so it is almost impossible to be controlled, but it doesn't hide the danger, and if someone is foolish enough to summon one of its beings to win the lottery, it's their fault. The Eternal and the Ladder, however, are far more insidious.<br /> <br /> The Ladder does not looks dangerous at first. Its demons are very obedient, and won't try to trick the summoner- after all, they come from a realm were everything is decided and nothing is left for free will. There is a trick, however- for the thing about the Depth is that they are what they eat. They eat freedom, for they lack it in their system- but they can utilize that stolen freedom for their own needs. Give them enough freedom, and they could even break the spell you used to bind them- and then there is no one in heaven or hell to save you as they drain you into an hollow husk dedicated into &quot;building the Ladder&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Eternal, on the other hand, has dangerous of its own- after all, there is a reason its demons use death as a coin in their realm. When those beings feed, they take away your ending- your whole ending. You will not age for a single day. You cells simply stop dying from this moment forward- but as they don't die, they don't need to reproduce. That means that injuries don't naturally heal. Magic may help, but its help is temporary at best. Every wound you suffer, every scratch or bump or broken nail- it will never heal. Every disease you suffer from won't stop trying to kill you. Every stretched muscle or sunburn would never, every go away. Eventually, body parts start falling apart, as the number of wounds exceed the tolerance of the mortal coil- but it doesn't stop you from feeling them. The pain never goes away. Even if someone where to grind you body or burn you to ash, you would still be alive. You will suffer from all eternity in the form of dust in the wind, unable to communicate with the world, unable to die, bound in pain which would turn your mind into living hell. <br /> <br /> Don't make bargains with the Depths, children. No matter how nice they look, their number one goal would always be to bite you in the ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T14:46:34-08:00","id":1426861,"title":"","content":"<br /> The Painting is a world that lacks a third dimension, it's inhabitants live out lives where lines become insurmountable and their cursed hearts jerk sideways like knives. The demons summoned the the mortal realm exist only in two dimensions and quickly go mad in our world. Unable to relate to something so completely outside their own existence. Going there is a trip to agony and insanity.<br /> The Infinite, lacks the concept of limits everything goes on forever without end or reason. When they manage to slip into our reality behind the stars and underneath black holes they steal the limits to make themselves comprehensible if only for a short time and leave whatever they stole in endlessness.<br /> The futility is a realm without purpose, everything just exists without any meaning or goal the demons here come to this world to find meaning and reason for their actions, the people and things that lose their purpose quickly fall to pieces or commit suicide.<br /> The present lacks the concept of the future. The demons here only do things that make sense in the moment or in the past and as such nothing has changed and they undergo terrible famines every winter that is completely unexpected while revenge seekers drift aimlessly around hoping to find the people who took their loved ones away.<br /> The garden lacks the concept of sin, the demons here commit the worst atrocities without remorse as innocent as the newest babe. When the steal the sin from others they either break down into formless sobbing at what they have done and the people who lack sin become the worst monsters imaginable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T17:25:33-08:00","id":1426885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laguz 24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1426861#post1426861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Painting is a world that lacks a third dimension, it's inhabitants live out lives where lines become insurmountable and their cursed hearts jerk sideways like knives. The demons summoned the the mortal realm exist only in two dimensions and quickly go mad in our world. Unable to relate to something so completely outside their own existence. Going there is a trip to agony and insanity.<br /> The Infinite, lacks the concept of limits everything goes on forever without end or reason. When they manage to slip into our reality behind the stars and underneath black holes they steal the limits to make themselves comprehensible if only for a short time and leave whatever they stole in endlessness.<br /> The futility is a realm without purpose, everything just exists without any meaning or goal the demons here come to this world to find meaning and reason for their actions, the people and things that lose their purpose quickly fall to pieces or commit suicide.<br /> The present lacks the concept of the future. The demons here only do things that make sense in the moment or in the past and as such nothing has changed and they undergo terrible famines every winter that is completely unexpected while revenge seekers drift aimlessly around hoping to find the people who took their loved ones away.<br /> The garden lacks the concept of sin, the demons here commit the worst atrocities without remorse as innocent as the newest babe. When the steal the sin from others they either break down into formless sobbing at what they have done and the people who lack sin become the worst monsters imaginable.</div> </div> </div> </div>the painting reminds me of two things. <br /> <br /> 1. flatland (obviously) <br /> <br /> 2. bill ciphers home, &quot;A world of flat lives and flat dreams.&quot; (might be misqouting)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T08:20:56-08:00","id":1426986,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to mention that the game The Void, by Ice Pick Lodge, is a perfect example of a Lower Depth lacking sympathy, both mundane and magical. Its absolutely fascinating, although I won't say more because uncovering the Mystery is the core of the experience.<br /> <br /> On a side note, their games have a very Mage feel to them. Especially Pathologic 2, which feels like a Mystery Play (the Polyhedron being the Watchtower), a high Opacity Mystery or even an Emanation. <br /> <br /> I highly recommend picking them up for inspiration. They are brimming with symbolism, mystery and fascinating worldbuilding. They are usually pretty cheap and especially so in Steam sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T17:46:26-08:00","id":1427229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1157565#post1157565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most spirits take an additive or consumptive approach to dealing with their competition \u2014 if they engage with other spirits, it's under the auspices of a derived relationship. (It's why magath are so messed up.)<br /> <br /> Wounded spirits don't incorporate their kills. The losing Resonance just goes nowhere because the spirit has become host to a hole in the fabric of the world's symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am not convinced yet that the Maeljin come from the Lower Depths. Regardless:<br /> <br /> The Purged Library: ask their denizens and they will tell you this place lacks stories. Ask the creatures of the Supernal or of other divine realms and they will tell you the same. How misleading. When the hundredth demon says &quot;stories&quot; they don't explain still what that element actually is, leaving one to assume that they are talking about ideas in minds and books. What they really mean is the continuity of time itself. Separating the infinite possibilities into &quot;happened&quot; and &quot;did not happen&quot;, and binding different events into a coherent whole.<br /> <br /> Just as your arm is a part of you, your past is a part of you too. When your arm is amputated it is no longer a part of you, and the same with your past as this place shreds your time. Past events are loosed into the present as separate entities and phenomena and their marks on their present versions will disappear. Random possibilities from stillborn timelines invade as the boundaries of canon break down.<br /> <br /> This world is endless static: which is endless, muted, impotent possibilities. Only able to coalesce as they dissolve our world, then inevitably break down again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T02:23:40-08:00","id":1427253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1427229#post1427229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not convinced yet that the Maeljin come from the Lower Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in not convinced they fit the bill as Lower Depths entities? 'Cause canon-wise I think it's pretty explicit. At least in first edition. Iirc Shunned by the Moon made Maeljin much more tailored towards WtF and the Shadow so I'm not sure they could be conclusively said to be of the Inferno anymore. Or maybe I'm just wrong about that. It was a while since I read either Inferno or SbtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T02:50:16-08:00","id":1427254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1427253#post1427253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Cause canon-wise I think it's pretty explicit. At least in first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Though the books are explicit that it's not canon exactly. The Maeljin are demons for the purposes of Inferno (not quite sure what they were going for with that wording). The Inferno <i>might</i> be Abaddon from Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T03:10:36-08:00","id":1427255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1427254#post1427254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inferno <i>might</i> be Abaddon from Imperial Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>No &quot;might&quot; about it. The former Mage lead dev even states as much in this very thread. The only weirdness about that is that IM is written with the now retconned assumption that Abaddon/Inferno <i>is</i> the Lower Depths rather than just being one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T04:42:33-08:00","id":1427262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1156813-homebrew-some-lower-depths?p=1427255#post1427255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No &quot;might&quot; about it. The former Mage lead dev even states as much in this very thread. The only weirdness about that is that IM is written with the now retconned assumption that Abaddon/Inferno <i>is</i> the Lower Depths rather than just being one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using 'might' in the sense of it's left open if it is in your game. I'm not disputing that that's clearly the intention.<br /> <br /> From IM pg. 8:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World of Darkness: Inferno <i>might</i> describe akathartoi from the Lower Depths. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T01:30:51-08:00","id":1427681,"title":"","content":"We were rather nervous when writing IM about its &quot;canonicity&quot;, given Mage had no line developer and had in fact already published a &quot;goodbye&quot; letter from Bill effectively ending the game line. We outlined the thing as though it would be sold as a set of three pdfs, in the manner of the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide or Glories of the Most High for Exalted. Plus, its subject matter could be taken as Mage laying down the settings for other lines, which was not our intention.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's why it's sometimes slightly less... Assuredly declarative than other books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T02:20:12-08:00","id":1427684,"title":"","content":"CofD on a whole is also a toolbox type of setting where each piece of setting information is optional despite the vast majority being designed to fit a singular &quot;canon&quot;, so to say. Sometimes the books basically include reminders about how things are optional and that you're free to use them in other ways even though they're intended to fit in a certain way.<br /> Since it's a pain in the ass to declare that you assume most setting information to be true whenever you want to discuss the setting, it's easier to just assume that it is for the purposes of any given discussion unless noted otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T13:58:22-08:00","id":1429981,"title":"","content":"Lots of very interesting ideas here, even though i play &amp; ST primarily Requiem. Never really toyed with it, but reading on the concept of &quot;dead universes, inhabited by alien beings hungry for certain aspects of our own existence&quot; definitely piqued my interest and i did conceive a critter out of this, the Face Stealers, entities that drain a person's form, memory &amp; capabilities to then assume their place, while keeping the weakened and confused originals caged but well-feed, so they may preserve those identities, at least for a time. An awful paradox in that to live on as a person the Face Stealer must regularly confront the lie that makes its identity possible.<br /> <br /> Way i imagined them they were <b><i>defined </i></b>by this pathetic conundrum of desiring life &amp; identity as a person more than anything, the hunger to be <i>somebody</i>, <i>anybody</i>, but the deeper they dig into this humanity, the more aware (and somewhat resentful) of the lie and monstrosity involved in its preservation they become. There were two little extras/twists to the dynamic too.<br /> <br /> - In truth, a Face Stealer <i>may </i>become &quot;the mask&quot; permanently through willpower sacrifice,but very few do due to the insecurities and doubts generated by their own condition (also, they do have a kernel of identity in Virtues &amp; Vices of their own, what might generate some inner conflict with the identity taken and relate in no small part to the whole cycle of self-doubt so common to these beings). For those that <b>do</b> take that bold step, even the memory of once being something else is lost turning fully into that individual.<br /> <br /> - A ironic colateral of the Face Stealer's regular feeding is that their victims slowly becomes ever more like the creature in many ways, what also results in the possibility of a dying victim, if somehow self-aware or still strong-willed enough, to spend permanent willpower to become a Face Stealer itself, angry and hungry for consuming and undoing the face of its suffering to the point of <b><i>denying its own existence</i></b> for the sake of payback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-30-2021, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}